# Expectation record for 14_abi_calling_convention/001_many_integer_parameters.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 001_many_integer_parameters
area               = 14_abi_calling_convention
description        = Integer parameter lists long enough to exhaust every target's argument registers and force stack spill: two lists of fifteen integer-class parameters each -- fifteen int values in the first, and fourteen long long values plus one trailing int variant tag in the second -- with the first list's fifteenth int likewise serving as its variant tag, so each list carries fourteen observed data values; each list is called in a folded and a volatile-runtime variant through a volatile function pointer, with every one of the fourteen data parameters printed individually
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour by construction. Only int, long long and
const char * appear in this program: there is no floating type, no aggregate, no union, no
bit-field, no unsigned type and no plain char used as a value, so whole classes of
undefined behaviour cannot arise here rather than merely being avoided.

- Fifteen integer-class parameters are passed to each callee -- FOURTEEN DATA VALUES plus a
  trailing int that selects the variant tag -- which exceeds the widest integer argument
  register file of the four supported ABIs, so every target marshals part of the argument
  list on the stack. Every parameter is declared and passed with a type that matches its
  argument exactly, and every one of the fourteen DATA parameters is printed back
  individually and in order; the fifteenth is the tag, and it appears in the output as the
  variant name every line carries rather than as a value of its own, so a tag delivered to
  the wrong slot renames every line of the group and is equally visible. No value is ever
  summarised into a checksum, because a checksum can mask two compensating errors while one
  argument delivered to the wrong slot and another delivered to its place is exactly the
  defect this program exists to catch.
- Only int and long long are passed or printed, both of which are the same width on all four
  targets.
- No signed integer overflow: no arithmetic whatever is performed on any parameter. Every
  integer value passed or printed is either a literal or a value read from statically
  initialised storage, and every one is far inside the range of its type -- the int values
  lie between -1014 and 1013, and the long long values within +/-5000000014, against a
  guaranteed long long range of at least +/-9223372036854775807.
- The single conversion in the program is well defined and value-preserving: the trailing
  argument of the runtime long long call is the explicit cast (int)plain_llong[14], applied
  to the value 1, which is representable in int. It is written as an explicit cast rather
  than left implicit so the narrowing is visible in the source and the strict warning gate
  has nothing to diagnose.
- No shift operator, no division and no remainder operator appears anywhere, so no shift
  count can be out of range and no division by zero is possible.
- No read of uninitialised storage: both volatile source arrays have static initialisers,
  and each plain staging array is filled completely by a bounded loop over all fifteen
  elements before any element of it is read.
- No object is modified twice between sequence points, and no argument list contains a side
  effect at all.
- Nothing depends on padding bytes or on alignment: sizeof never appears in the program, no
  object is inspected byte-wise, and no aggregate exists to have padding.
- Nothing depends on the relative addresses of unrelated objects, and no address or pointer
  value is printed. The only pointer values in the program are the two function pointers,
  which are called rather than printed, and the const char * variant tag, which is printed
  as the string it designates and never as an address.
- No default argument promotion is relied upon at any call: both callees are declared with
  full prototypes before use, so every argument is converted to its declared parameter type.
  The only variadic calls are to printf, and each conversion specification matches its
  argument's type exactly after promotion -- %d for int, %lld for long long, %s for
  const char *.
- printf is declared by hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);` and no header is included,
  because the compiler under test ships no stdio.h; an #include <stdio.h> would fail against
  it while succeeding against the reference compiler and would manufacture a divergence
  caused by the test rather than by the compiler.
- The two-variant rule is applied throughout: a folded variant whose arguments are
  compile-time constants, and a runtime variant whose arguments are read from volatile
  storage so the values are genuinely materialised and marshalled rather than folded into the
  callee. Without the second variant, optimisation would substitute the folder's answer for
  the backend's at -O1 and -O2 and an argument-marshalling defect would escape entirely.
- Nothing is allocated, nothing outside the translation unit is read, and main returns 0,
  which is inside the permitted 0-125 range for an expected exit status. No socket, no file,
  no environment variable, no clock and no random source is touched: every input to the
  program is a literal in its own source.

- NOTHING DEPENDS ON UNSPECIFIED EVALUATION ORDER, and it is enforced structurally rather
  than argued. An access to a volatile object is an observable side effect, and C11
  6.5.2.2p10 leaves the order of evaluation of a call's function designator, of its
  arguments, and of subexpressions within those arguments unspecified. So the runtime
  variants STAGE every volatile datum before any call: each element of vint and vllong is
  copied into plain array storage in a bounded loop, one volatile read per iteration and per
  full expression, and the calls then pass only those plain elements. The one remaining
  volatile access in a call expression is the call-boundary function pointer itself, which
  is a single access and therefore has no order to be unspecified. Staging costs no
  discriminating power: a value that arrived through a volatile load stays opaque to the
  optimizer, so every argument is still materialised at run time and marshalled through the
  ABI.

- THE CALL BOUNDARY IS MADE HARD TO OPTIMIZE AWAY, WHICH IS NOT THE SAME AS BEING GUARANTEED
  BY THE LANGUAGE, and the two are stated apart here because conflating them would overclaim
  what this program proves. Each callee is reached through a volatile-qualified function
  pointer. WHAT ISO C REQUIRES of that: an access to a volatile object is a side effect and
  part of the observable behaviour an implementation must reproduce (C11 5.1.2.3p2 and p6),
  and C11 6.7.3p7 requires an expression referring to a volatile-qualified object to be
  evaluated strictly according to the abstract machine's rules -- so the pointer must be
  RE-READ at each point of call and control must be transferred to whatever function that
  particular load produced. WHAT ISO C DOES NOT REQUIRE: that the transfer reaches the
  callee's original entry point. An implementation may legally introduce a specialised clone,
  scalarise a copy of the body, or perform guarded devirtualization -- compare the loaded
  pointer against a known function and call a specialised entry on the matching path -- and
  still honour the loaded value, because the observable behaviour is unchanged. An earlier
  form of this paragraph asserted that the signature "may not be cloned or scalarised", which
  is stronger than anything the standard says and is withdrawn.
- SO THE BOUNDARY IS AN OPTIMIZATION OBSTACLE, VERIFIED ON NAMED ARTIFACTS RATHER THAN
  ASSERTED AS A LANGUAGE RULE. Measured on the committed source with gcc 13.4.0 at -O2 on all
  four reference drivers: both callees are still emitted out of line under their own labels;
  no specialised clone appears anywhere -- zero symbols carrying .constprop, .isra or .part.
  -- and each variant reaches its callee through a genuine indirect transfer, four such sites
  per target (call *%reg on x86_64 and i686, blr on aarch64, jalr on riscv64). Without the
  indirection the obstacle is absent: an ordinary static callee is free to be inlined at -O1
  and -O2, and a callee that is inlined marshals nothing at all, so the parameter passing this
  program claims to exercise would not happen.
- THE RESIDUAL RISK IS RECORDED RATHER THAN PAPERED OVER. Those measurements are evidence
  about the reference compiler's artifacts, not a property every compiler under test must have.
  A compiler that devirtualizes through a specialised entry could route a cell past the
  register assignments argued above while still printing the same bytes, and this program would
  not detect that. Closing it would take a per-cell STATIC check of the artifact the compiler
  under test emitted -- an indirect transfer present, no specialised clone of either callee --
  which is a harness capability this suite does not have and which no oracle here substitutes
  for. Until it exists, the honest statement is that the indirection makes the boundary very
  likely on any optimizing compiler and is verified for the reference toolchain.
- THE MECHANISM IS DELIBERATELY PURE ISO C -- a volatile function pointer and nothing more --
  rather than a function attribute, because the documented attribute set of the compiler under
  test is packed, aligned, section, unused, deprecated, visibility and format
  (docs/technical-specifications.md line 506), so an inlining attribute would risk a divergence
  caused by the test and would import an extension into an area whose subject is the calling
  convention.

Verified rather than asserted: the default strict warning gate (-Wall -Wextra -pedantic
-Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror) produces zero diagnostics in the single
native compile-only invocation the suite makes of it; the sanitizer gate
(-fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all) runs to completion in its one
instrumented native build with no diagnostic and exit status 0; and all twelve cells of the
declared matrix produce byte-identical stdout of 1400 bytes over 56 lines with exit status 0
and an empty standard error.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This area exists because the four backends implement four different application binary
interfaces, and it is the densest concentration of cross-backend divergence surface in the
corpus. The parameter counts are sized against the WIDEST register file rather than the
narrowest - eight integer registers on AAPCS64 (x0-x7) and LP64D (a0-a7), six on System V
AMD64 (rdi, rsi, rdx, rcx, r8, r9), and none on System V i386 cdecl, which marshals
everything on the stack - so every target genuinely spills and no target is left exercising
only its register path. Confirmed at instruction level in the reference compiler's -O2
assembly: x86_64 passes six arguments in registers and pushes the remaining nine, i686
pushes all fifteen, and
aarch64 and riscv64 each fill their eight argument registers and store the remaining seven
to the outgoing argument area. The same inspection confirms the enforced call boundary
holds on every target - four indirect calls per target, through `call *%rax` on x86_64,
`call *%eax` on i686, `blr` on aarch64 and `jalr` on riscv64, with both callee bodies still
present as real functions rather than inlined away.

The measured target differences are handled by construction, so no target restriction and no
marker is needed:

1. sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) are 4 on i686 and 8 on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64
   (docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457-462). Width normalisation is therefore
   absolute here: only int and long long are passed or printed, and both were measured at 4
   and 8 bytes respectively on all four targets. No long, no size_t, no ptrdiff_t and no
   pointer value appears in the output, and the conversion specifications are exactly %d,
   %lld and %s - %ld, %lu, %zu and %p never appear. The long long values deliberately exceed
   the 32-bit range, so i686 must marshal each of them as a register or stack pair rather
   than as a single word, which is the divergence surface that type is here to cover.
2. Plain char signedness is implementation-defined and was measured signed on x86_64 and
   i686 and unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64. No plain char is passed or printed as a value:
   char occurs in this program only as const char *, for the printf format string and for
   the variant tag, and a tag is printed as the string it designates, so the signedness
   difference cannot reach the output.
3. long double has three representations across the four targets (measured 16, 12, 16 and 16
   bytes). No floating type of any width is used here - the program contains no float, no
   double and no long double - so neither the representation difference nor i686's x87
   evaluation of intermediates can affect this program. long double belongs to
   13_floating_point/004_long_double_target_restricted, which is where it is compared.
4. Aggregate size, layout and padding cannot affect this program, because it declares no
   struct and no union at all and never applies sizeof. Aggregate parameter passing is
   covered by 004_small_and_large_struct_passing and 005_struct_return_by_value, where the
   layout differences are handled with their own recorded reasons.
5. All four targets are little-endian, and in any case no byte-order-sensitive value is
   printed: every value reaches stdout through a conversion specification rather than through
   a byte-wise inspection of its storage.

Because every printed value is width-independent and representation-independent, cross-target
output identity holds by construction rather than by coincidence; it was then confirmed by
measurement over all twelve cells. Oracle (b) therefore stays enabled for this program, and a
cross-backend divergence here would be a genuine finding rather than an implementation-defined
difference.
END
